WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:01:27.916 --> 00:01:33.041
So we just checked in at our
hotel here at the Grand Hyatt Jeju

00:01:33.458 --> 00:01:36.833
and the room is
spectacular in my opinion.

00:01:36.916 --> 00:01:40.333
Paid a little bit extra for the
ocean view and I think it's worth it.

00:01:40.416 --> 00:01:42.541
And you can even see
like some incoming planes

00:01:42.625 --> 00:01:45.500
landing at the Jeju airport 
which is pretty cool.

00:01:46.041 --> 00:01:50.375
So after landing in Jeju, we picked up 
our rental car which was an EV

00:01:51.083 --> 00:01:53.291
decided to go with the IONIQ 5

00:01:53.291 --> 00:01:56.833
and yeah, it's really just a pleasure to drive.

00:01:57.500 --> 00:02:00.333
I was a little bit concerned about 
EV and charging

00:02:00.333 --> 00:02:01.708
but if you're staying in the Grand Hyatt,

00:02:02.250 --> 00:02:04.948
there's free parking, of course,
if you're staying as a hotel guest

00:02:04.948 --> 00:02:08.416
but there's also loads of EV charging spots

00:02:08.416 --> 00:02:10.684
that you can use 
which makes it super convenient

00:02:10.684 --> 00:02:12.643
if you decide to go with an EV.

00:02:12.833 --> 00:02:15.500
Other than that, it's been
a pleasure to drive around Jeju.

00:02:15.583 --> 00:02:18.708
It's obviously a lot
less chaotic than Seoul or Busan.

00:02:18.791 --> 00:02:21.875
If you're like used to
driving in like big cities

00:02:21.875 --> 00:02:24.708
Like this should be easy for you 
I would say.

00:02:24.708 --> 00:02:26.791
You know nothing compared to 
Seoul whatsoever.

00:05:15.291 --> 00:05:18.958
Alright so we are just outside of Saebil

00:05:18.958 --> 00:05:22.250
Saebil, which is like a cafe here in Jeju

00:05:22.250 --> 00:05:25.625
and right outside the cafe 
there's this pink muhly

00:05:26.083 --> 00:05:28.291
It's called Mule or Muhly Grass

00:05:28.291 --> 00:05:29.708
and we're taking some photos, 
taking some footage

00:05:29.916 --> 00:05:32.291
Looks really beautiful,
it's really hot still though

00:05:32.500 --> 00:05:37.000
It might not seem that way but
it's pretty warm, it's pretty humid so

00:05:37.708 --> 00:05:40.750
But yeah, you gotta do
what you gotta do for some content

00:06:06.625 --> 00:06:10.791
First time having Hallabong tangerine,

00:06:10.791 --> 00:06:11.916
I believe it's tangerine,

00:06:11.916 --> 00:06:13.208
tangerine juice

00:06:16.083 --> 00:06:19.375
Ooh, okay it's
different, it's a lot more zingy

00:06:20.083 --> 00:06:22.083
It's a lot less orangey.

00:06:22.083 --> 00:06:24.708
I expected it to be more like 
orange juice,

00:06:24.958 --> 00:06:26.041
it's a lot more lighter

00:07:04.416 --> 00:07:05.375
What's up babe?

00:07:05.583 --> 00:07:06.416
What are you looking at?

00:07:07.041 --> 00:07:08.375
Are you looking for snakes?

00:08:37.333 --> 00:08:40.625
We just climbed Seongsan Ilchulbong

00:08:40.791 --> 00:08:42.375
which is the sunrise peak.

00:08:42.458 --> 00:08:43.333
This is obviously not sunrise.

00:08:43.791 --> 00:08:46.791
Couldn't be bothered to
wake up that early to do the hike,

00:08:46.875 --> 00:08:48.125
but I kinda regret it now

00:08:48.208 --> 00:08:49.958
because it's super hot and humid up here.

00:08:50.333 --> 00:08:52.625
But other than that, it's
not that difficult to get up here.

00:08:52.708 --> 00:08:53.541
I don't think it's that tough,

00:08:53.625 --> 00:08:55.500
especially if you're used
to hiking or anything like that.

00:08:55.583 --> 00:08:56.250
It's really not that bad.

00:08:56.333 --> 00:08:57.250
It's just a lot of steps.

00:08:58.208 --> 00:09:01.208
So if you're a Stairmaster, master,

00:09:01.958 --> 00:09:02.708
you can probably make it.

00:09:03.041 --> 00:09:05.708
And the views up here, I
mean, pretty decent, pretty great.

00:09:05.791 --> 00:09:08.666
I think it's probably
better during the sunrise hour.

00:09:09.208 --> 00:09:10.416
But still it's worth coming up here

00:09:10.791 --> 00:09:12.125
and getting some nice photos.

00:09:12.375 --> 00:09:14.291
You can see the
large, green sort of crater.

00:09:14.750 --> 00:09:16.666
No lake though, like for example,

00:09:17.000 --> 00:09:18.209
Hallasan, there's a lake on top.

00:09:18.209 --> 00:09:21.291
But I don't think it's necessary 
because you're a crater

00:09:21.458 --> 00:09:23.291
and then you'll have a lake.

00:09:23.583 --> 00:09:24.916
But still, there's no lake up here.

00:09:25.000 --> 00:09:25.917
It's very green.

00:09:25.917 --> 00:09:28.500
Just a green volcanic crater.

00:09:28.583 --> 00:09:29.500
It's been a great little hike.

00:09:29.750 --> 00:09:31.875
And just enjoying the view here with Lisa

00:09:32.750 --> 00:09:33.250
for a bit

00:09:33.250 --> 00:09:34.625
before we descend down.

00:10:50.208 --> 00:10:52.250
Another day, another cafe.

00:14:02.458 --> 00:14:04.416
Yeah, just your regular lobster

00:14:05.083 --> 00:14:06.916
Not, not anything special

00:14:07.083 --> 00:14:09.000
But, you know, I'm all there for the show

00:14:09.083 --> 00:14:09.875
The show was awesome,

00:14:09.958 --> 00:14:11.875
the guys showed a lot of showmanship

00:14:12.083 --> 00:14:14.541
So, five out of ten

00:14:15.083 --> 00:14:16.166
for the lobster

00:14:17.083 --> 00:14:19.083
And ten out of ten for the showmanship,

00:14:19.166 --> 00:14:19.666
definitely.

00:15:44.208 --> 00:15:45.750
Do I need some therapy?

00:16:41.583 --> 00:16:42.791
Happy, happy, happy...

00:17:39.166 --> 00:17:41.041
Is it good? Is it really good?

00:17:47.583 --> 00:17:48.625
After a long day of driving,

00:17:49.291 --> 00:17:53.500
in this humid,
warm weather we got in Jeju,

00:17:54.083 --> 00:17:56.375
nothing beats fresh juice

00:17:57.208 --> 00:17:58.541
from this tangerine.

00:18:06.166 --> 00:18:06.916
More!

00:18:07.833 --> 00:18:08.583
More, more, more!

00:21:18.041 --> 00:21:19.541
Hey, what's up everyone. This is Allan

00:21:19.708 --> 00:21:21.333
and that's the end of my

00:21:21.500 --> 00:21:24.708
Korea vlog series, 
if you can call it that.

00:21:24.958 --> 00:21:28.000
I was really happy
to be able to visit Jeju

00:21:28.000 --> 00:21:31.291
And I just love these
more road trip kind of trips

00:21:31.375 --> 00:21:33.375
Just having more freedom to explore

00:21:33.458 --> 00:21:35.375
and go where you want, when you want

00:21:35.458 --> 00:21:37.041
is just my cup of tea.

00:21:37.291 --> 00:21:39.708
But yeah, I can't wait to share more

00:21:39.791 --> 00:21:41.791
about my Korea trip

00:21:41.875 --> 00:21:43.875
But up next is going to be

00:21:43.958 --> 00:21:46.083
a travel guide to Korea

00:21:46.333 --> 00:21:48.208
Just packing everything that I've learned

00:21:48.291 --> 00:21:50.500
and experienced while traveling here

00:21:50.750 --> 00:21:52.250
In a sort of neat package

00:21:52.333 --> 00:21:55.208
for anyone who's planning 
to visit Korea themselves

00:21:55.875 --> 00:21:59.583
So that's currently on
the editing table as we speak.

00:21:59.666 --> 00:22:01.166
But overall, Korea was great

00:22:01.250 --> 00:22:04.166
and it will certainly not be my last trip.

00:22:04.250 --> 00:22:06.208
And finally, I just want to say

00:22:06.291 --> 00:22:09.750
thank you for sticking
around to the end of this video

00:22:10.083 --> 00:22:11.083
This is Allan.

00:22:11.083 --> 00:22:13.500
I'll see you guys in the next one.

